# Security Baseline

- Never commit secrets. Use env vars / secret managers. Add `.env*` to `.gitignore` (except `.env.example`).
- Validate and sanitize all untrusted input at system boundaries.
- Use parameterized queries / ORM APIs — never string-concatenate SQL.
- Escape or sanitize HTML to prevent XSS; prefer framework defaults (React JSX escaping).
- Enforce authz on every sensitive route/action — not only on the UI.
- Set secure cookie flags (`HttpOnly`, `Secure`, `SameSite`) for session cookies.
- Prefer least-privilege IAM and scoped API tokens.
- Log security-relevant events; never log passwords, tokens, or full PII unnecessarily.
- Dependency updates: pin versions thoughtfully; review high-severity CVEs before shipping.
